    workbook: ['Company ABC 2025 challenge: net loss €219,165; depreciation €66,665; provisions €80,000; receivables increase €830,000; inventory increase €930,000; payables increase €870,000; other liabilities increase €50,000; equipment investment €445,000; new loans €1,050,000; share capital issued €500,000. Build CFO, CFI, CFF and the net cash movement. Reconcile to closing cash and explain each working-capital sign.', 'CFO = −219,165 + 66,665 + 80,000 − 830,000 − 930,000 + 870,000 + 50,000 = −€912,500. CFI = −€445,000. CFF = 1,050,000 + 500,000 = €1,550,000. Net cash movement = −912,500 − 445,000 + 1,550,000 = €192,500, matching closing cash where opening cash is zero. Receivables and inventory growth use cash; payables and other liabilities growth temporarily conserve cash.']
