    workbook: ['Using Joe’s Gadgets (2016 → 2017): current assets €7.0m → €11.05m; inventory €2m → €4m; current liabilities €4.5m → €7m; COGS €6m → €11m; receivables €2m → €4m; sales €15m → €20m; fixed assets €10m → €11m; total assets €17m → €22.05m. Compute current ratio, quick ratio, inventory turnover, DSO on 365 days, fixed-asset turnover and total-asset turnover for both years. State which changes warrant investigation.', '2016 → 2017: current ratio = 7/4.5 = 1.56 → 11.05/7 = 1.58. Quick ratio = (7−2)/4.5 = 1.11 → (11.05−4)/7 = 1.01. Inventory turnover = 6/2 = 3.00 → 11/4 = 2.75 times. DSO = 2/15×365 = 48.7 → 4/20×365 = 73 days. Fixed-asset turnover = 15/10 = 1.50 → 20/11 = 1.82; total-asset turnover = 15/17 = 0.88 → 20/22.05 = 0.91. Investigate slower collections and inventory movement; year-end balances and seasonality can affect the ratios.']
